WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.562
First, which cloud.

2
00:00:01.562 --> 00:00:05.466
A GCC tenant keeps the worldwide
Microsoft Graph endpoint,

3
00:00:05.466 --> 00:00:09.529
so this workbook's baseline reads
graph dot microsoft dot com.

4
00:00:09.529 --> 00:00:13.513
Microsoft Learn's national cloud
page gives GCC High and the

5
00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:17.337
Defense Department their own
hosts, a short side note here.

6
00:00:17.337 --> 00:00:18.424
Why does it matter?

7
00:00:18.424 --> 00:00:20.737
Because a wrong cloud fails silently.

8
00:00:20.737 --> 00:00:25.408
A GCC High tenant read on the
worldwide host simply returns nothing,

9
00:00:25.408 --> 00:00:27.826
and the gate passes on an empty list.

10
00:00:27.826 --> 00:00:30.582
So the kit has one row
per cloud and no default,

11
00:00:30.582 --> 00:00:35.710
and the live run refuses a Graph session
in another environment or another tenant.
